Course.start({"num":22,"unit":4,"slug":"m22-gustar","minutes":45,"title":"El verbo gustar","subtitle":"Me gusta, me gustan; indirect object pronouns; encantar","lede":"Spanish doesn't say *I like chocolate*. It says *chocolate is pleasing to me*: **Me gusta el chocolate.** Once you see the pattern, it's simple.","recap":"Last time you learned irregular yo forms (*hago, pongo, salgo, sé, conozco*) and the difference between **saber** and **conocer**.","context":{"title":"Un regalo de cacao","place":"Guatemala · España, 1544","text":"For thousands of years before Europeans arrived, people in Mexico and Central America drank **chocolate**, made from roasted **cacao** beans. The Maya and Aztecs drank it bitter, often with chili, and used cacao beans as money.\n\nThe first time chocolate is recorded in Spain is **1544**. A group of **Q'eqchi' Maya** nobles from Guatemala traveled across the ocean with Dominican friars to visit the young Prince Philip. Among their gifts were jars of beaten chocolate. Over the next century, Spaniards added sugar and cinnamon, and chocolate became the favorite drink of Europe.\n\nToday in Spain, people dip **churros** in thick hot chocolate. And most people would agree: {{Me gusta mucho el chocolate.}} *I like chocolate a lot*, or literally, *Chocolate pleases me a lot.*"},"learn":[{"title":"Gusta or gustan?","text":"With **gustar**, the thing you like is the subject. If it's **one thing** or an **activity** (an infinitive), use **gusta**. If it's **more than one thing**, use **gustan**.","examples":[["Me gusta el chocolate.","I like chocolate. (one thing)"],["Me gustan las frutas.","I like fruit. (more than one)"],["Me gusta bailar.","I like to dance. (an activity)"],["No me gustan los tomates.","I don't like tomatoes."]],"tip":"With *gustar*, use **the**: *Me gusta **el** chocolate*, even when English doesn't (Module 7)."},{"title":"Who likes it? Indirect object pronouns","text":"The person who likes something is shown by a pronoun **before** the verb. To make it clear or to add emphasis, add **a** + a name or pronoun.","table":{"head":["Pronoun","Example","For clarity or emphasis"],"rows":[["**me** (to me)","{{Me gusta el arroz.}}","{{A mí me gusta el arroz.}}"],["**te** (to you)","{{¿Te gusta el arroz?}}","{{A ti te gusta…}}"],["**le** (to him, her, you formal)","{{Le gusta el arroz.}}","{{A Juan le gusta…}} · {{A usted le gusta…}}"],["**nos** (to us)","{{Nos gusta el arroz.}}","{{A nosotros nos gusta…}}"],["**os** (to you all, Spain)","{{Os gusta el arroz.}}","{{A vosotros os gusta…}}"],["**les** (to them, you all)","{{Les gusta el arroz.}}","{{A mis padres les gusta…}}"]],"caption":"**A mí** has an accent mark; **a ti** doesn't."},"tip":"To agree: {{A mí también.}} (*Me too.*) To agree with a negative: {{A mí tampoco.}} (*Me neither.*)"},{"title":"Verbs like gustar, and food","text":"**Encantar** (to love a thing or activity), **interesar** (to interest) and **importar** (to matter) work the same way: {{Me encantan los churros.}} {{Nos interesa la historia.}}","flash":[["el chocolate","chocolate"],["las frutas","fruit"],["las verduras","vegetables"],["el arroz","rice"],["los frijoles","beans"],["la carne","meat"],["los huevos","eggs"],["el helado","ice cream"],["las papas fritas","French fries"],["la ensalada","salad"],["los churros","churros"],["la paella","paella"]]}],"tasks":[{"id":"t1","type":"select","title":"Gusta or gustan?","intro":"Choose the right form.","items":[{"s":"Me {gusta|gustan} el chocolate."},{"s":"Me {gustan|gusta} los churros."},{"s":"¿Te {gusta|gustan} nadar?","why":"An activity (infinitive): **gusta**."},{"s":"A mi hermano le {gustan|gusta} los videojuegos."},{"s":"Nos {gusta|gustan} la música latina."},{"s":"No les {gustan|gusta} las verduras."},{"s":"Me {encantan|encanta} las papas fritas."},{"s":"A mis padres les {gusta|gustan} cocinar y bailar.","why":"Activities stay singular: **gusta**."}],"hints":["Look at what comes **after** *gustar*: one thing or an activity → **gusta**; more than one thing → **gustan**."]},{"id":"t2","type":"cloze","title":"Who likes it?","intro":"Write the pronoun: **me, te, le, nos, os** or **les**.","items":["A mí [me] gusta el helado.","¿A ti [te] gustan las frutas?","A Juan [le] gusta el fútbol.","A nosotros [nos] gustan los perros.","A mis abuelos [les] gusta caminar.","A usted [le] gusta el café, ¿verdad?","A vosotros [os] encanta la paella.","A Sofía y a mí [nos] interesa la historia."],"hints":["*A Sofía y a mí* = *to us*.","*Usted* uses **le**; *ustedes* uses **les**."]},{"id":"t3","type":"match","title":"La comida","intro":"Tap a Spanish food (you'll hear it), then its meaning.","pairs":[["las verduras","vegetables"],["el arroz","rice"],["los frijoles","beans"],["la carne","meat"],["los huevos","eggs"],["el helado","ice cream"],["las papas fritas","French fries"],["la ensalada","salad"]],"hints":["*Papas fritas* are fried potatoes."]},{"id":"t4","type":"order","title":"Build the sentences","intro":"Tap the words in order.","items":[{"en":"My brother likes dogs.","es":"A mi hermano le gustan los perros."},{"en":"We love to dance.","es":"Nos encanta bailar.","alt":["A nosotros nos encanta bailar."]},{"en":"Do you (tú) like tomatoes?","es":"¿Te gustan los tomates?","extra":["gusta"]},{"en":"I don't like vegetables.","es":"No me gustan las verduras."}],"hints":["The pronoun goes before *gusta(n)*; *no* goes before the pronoun: **No me gustan…**","*Tomates* is plural: **gustan**."]},{"id":"t5","type":"listen","title":"¿Qué les gusta?","intro":"Listen and answer.","questions":[{"say":"Me encantan los churros con chocolate, pero no me gusta el café.","q":"What doesn't the speaker like?","choices":[["coffee",true],["churros",false],["chocolate",false],["tea",false]]},{"say":"A mi hermana le gusta leer, y a mí me gusta jugar al fútbol.","q":"What does the sister like?","choices":[["reading",true],["soccer",false],["cooking",false],["music",false]]},{"say":"A nosotros nos gustan las frutas, sobre todo las fresas.","q":"Which fruit do they like most?","choices":[["strawberries",true],["apples",false],["bananas",false],["oranges",false]]},{"say":"—No me gustan las verduras. —A mí tampoco.","q":"What does the second person mean?","choices":[["They don't like vegetables either.",true],["They love vegetables.",false],["They like some vegetables.",false],["They want more vegetables.",false]]}],"hints":["*Tampoco* = *neither*."]},{"id":"t6","type":"translate","title":"Say it in Spanish","intro":"Translate.","items":[{"en":"I like ice cream.","es":["[a mí] me gusta el helado"]},{"en":"Do you (tú) like to read?","es":["¿[a ti] te gusta leer?"]},{"en":"She loves churros.","es":["[a ella] le encantan los churros"]},{"en":"We don't like beans.","es":["[a nosotros] no nos gustan los frijoles","a nosotras no nos gustan los frijoles"]},{"en":"My parents like to cook.","es":["a mis padres les gusta cocinar"]}],"hints":["*I like X* = **Me gusta(n) X**.","*Loves* (a thing) = **encanta(n)**."]},{"id":"s1","type":"speak","title":"Say it out loud","intro":"Listen, record, compare.","items":[{"s":"Me gusta mucho el chocolate."},{"s":"¿Te gustan los churros? A mí me encantan."},{"s":"A mí tampoco."}]}],"build":{"heading":"Lo que me gusta","prompt":"Write **at least 6 sentences** about foods and activities that you and others like, love and don't like. Use **gusta** and **gustan**, at least one **le** or **les** (another person), **encanta** or **encantan**, and one **negative**.","model":"{{Me gusta mucho la pizza.}} {{Me encantan las papas fritas.}} {{No me gustan los tomates.}} {{A mi mamá le gusta cocinar arroz con frijoles.}} {{A mis hermanos les gustan los videojuegos.}} {{A todos nos gusta el helado de chocolate.}}","placeholder":"Me gusta…","reqs":[{"t":"At least 6 sentences","sentences":6},{"t":"**gusta** (one thing or an activity)","any":["gusta"]},{"t":"**gustan** (more than one thing)","any":["gustan"]},{"t":"Another person: **le** or **les** + gusta(n)","re":"\\b(le|les)\\s+(gusta|gustan|encanta|encantan|interesa|interesan)\\b"},{"t":"**encanta** or **encantan**","any":["encanta","encantan"]},{"t":"A negative: **no me gusta(n)…**","re":"\\bno\\s+(me|te|le|nos|os|les)\\s+(gusta|gustan|encanta|encantan|interesa|interesan)\\b"}]},"reflect":{"q":"Chocolate traveled from the Maya to Spain as a gift, and now people everywhere love it. What food from another culture do you love? What can sharing a meal teach people from different backgrounds about each other?","placeholder":"A food from another culture I love is…"},"further":{"id":"x1","type":"errors","title":"Challenge: fix the mistakes","intro":"Tap the wrong word, then type the correct one.","items":[{"s":"Me gustan el chocolate.","bad":"gustan","fix":"gusta"},{"s":"Le gusta las fresas.","bad":"gusta","fix":"gustan"},{"s":"A Juan me gusta correr.","bad":"me","fix":"le"},{"s":"Nos gustan jugar al tenis.","bad":"gustan","fix":"gusta"},{"s":"A mi también.","bad":"mi","fix":"mí","why":"*A mí* (me) has an accent."}]},"culture":"**¿Sabías?** The word *chocolate* probably comes from Nahuatl, the language of the Aztecs, and so do *tomate* (from *tomatl*) and *aguacate* (avocado, from *ahuacatl*).","unitTitle":"En la ciudad: verbos irregulares","code":"NDQ1MS1PQUNBQw==","prev":"m21-yo-irregular.html","next":"m23-reflexivos.html"});
